More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (421–430)
421. Improper Host Header Validation
Host Header Injection
Applications trust the Host header, allowing attackers to manipulate links, password reset URLs, or redirects.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
422. Insecure Password Reset Token
Password Reset Token Weakness
Password reset tokens are predictable or never expire.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
423. Improper Validation of Email Inputs
Email Input Validation Vulnerability
Email fields accept malicious payloads or scripts.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
424. API Endpoint Enumeration
API Endpoint Enumeration
Attackers can discover hidden API endpoints due to poor security controls.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
425. Insecure Cookie Storage
Cookie Storage Vulnerability
Sensitive cookies stored without Secure or HttpOnly flags.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
426. Improper Webhook Validation
Webhook Validation Failure
Webhooks accept requests from untrusted sources without verification.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
427. Unauthorized Access to User Profiles
User Profile Authorization Bypass
Users can access other users’ profiles or personal information.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
428. Improper Filtering of Special Characters
Special Character Injection
Applications fail to sanitize special characters in user input.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
429. Insecure API Pagination Controls
API Pagination Manipulation
Attackers manipulate pagination parameters to extract additional data.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
430. Unrestricted Resource Consumption
Denial of Service via Resource Exhaustion
Applications allow excessive requests or heavy operations that consume server resources.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
